{"name":"Ficus Elastica","hex":"#006131","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ficus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant belonging to the genus Ficus, including the rubber plant, of species Ficus elastica."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ficus"},{"term":"elastica","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A curve that minimizes bending energy; the shape that a thin flexible rod assumes when its endpoints are fixed.","Connective tissue that contains elastic fibers, such as that found in blood vessels or skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elastica"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ficus elastica","blocks":[{"text":"Ficus elastica, the rubber fig, rubber bush, rubber tree, rubber plant, or Indian rubber bush, Indian rubber tree, or rambung is a species of flowering plant in the family Moraceae, native to eastern parts of South and Southeast Asia. Its common names reflect its historical use as a source of rubber within its native range, but it is not used in the modern commercial-scale production of natural rubber."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Ficus_elastica_leaves_02.JPG/330px-Ficus_elastica_leaves_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ficus_elastica","wikidata":"Q160576"},{"title":"Ficus","blocks":[{"text":"Ficus is a genus of about 850 species of woody trees, shrubs, vines, epiphytes and hemiepiphytes in the family Moraceae. Collectively known as fig trees or figs, they are native throughout the tropics with a few species extending into the semi-warm temperate zone. Many Ficus species are grown for their fruits, though only two species, the common fig and sycamore fig, are cultivated to any extent, with common fig being the type species and by far the most important. The fruit of most other species are also edible though they are usually of only local economic importance or eaten as bushfood. However, they are extremely important food resources for wildlife. Figs are also of considerable cultural importance throughout the tropics, both as objects of worship and for their many practical uses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Sycomoros_old.jpg/330px-Sycomoros_old.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ficus","wikidata":"Q59798"},{"title":"Elastica","blocks":[{"text":"Elastica were an English rock band formed in London in 1992 by guitarist/singer Justine Frischmann and drummer Justin Welch after their departure from Suede. The band was stylistically influenced by punk rock, post-punk and new wave music. The band's members changed several times, with Frischmann and Welch being the only members who remained in Elastica from its formation to its dissolution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/21/Elastica_The_Menace_press_kit.jpg/330px-Elastica_The_Menace_press_kit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elastica","wikidata":"Q1060797"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/10_Shnongpdei_1.JPG/500px-10_Shnongpdei_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/10_Shnongpdei_1.JPG/1280px-10_Shnongpdei_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/10_Shnongpdei_1.JPG/500px-10_Shnongpdei_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial roots of Ficus elastica being formed into a bridge in Meghalaya, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A10_Shnongpdei_1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Ficus_elastica_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-